From: Fractal Microsystems <bsp@fractalmicro.org>
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: clamp virtual PCM channels before rejecting hardware limits

ALSA conversion PCMs can advertise 10000 channels. The existing virtual
PCM clamp handles this, but a hardware sanity check rejects the PCM first.
Keep that rejection for hardware only and let virtual PCMs reach the clamp.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/hostapi/alsa/pa_linux_alsa.c
+++ b/src/hostapi/alsa/pa_linux_alsa.c
@@ -904,7 +904,7 @@
     ENSURE_( alsa_snd_pcm_hw_params_get_channels_min( hwParams, &minChans ), paUnanticipatedHostError );
     ENSURE_( alsa_snd_pcm_hw_params_get_channels_max( hwParams, &maxChans ), paUnanticipatedHostError );
     const unsigned int kReasonableMaxChannels = 1024;
-    if( maxChans > kReasonableMaxChannels )
+    if( !isPlug && maxChans > kReasonableMaxChannels )
     {
         PA_DEBUG(( "%s: maxChans = %u, which is unreasonably high\n", __FUNCTION__, maxChans ));
         result = paUnanticipatedHostError;
